query people_by_age($min: I32) {
    match {
        $p: Person
        $p.age >= $min
    }
    return { $p.name, $p.age }
}

raw:
I can't write this query in edition-2 GQ, because the reference card has no arithmetic expressions. The filter operators are a closed list (`=`, `!=`, `<`, `>`, `<=`, `>=`, `in`, `contains`, `starts_with`, `is null`, `is not null`). Return items can only be properties, aggregates, or aliased comparisons. So `age * 2 >= $min`, `age * 2 as twice`, and `2026 - age as born_about` all have no valid spelling.

The closest valid query returns the raw age, and the doubling and subtraction have to be done by the caller:

```gq
query people_by_age($min: I32) {
    match {
        $p: Person
        $p.age >= $min
    }
    return { $p.name, $p.age }
}
```

This filters on `age >= $min`, not on doubled age. For an exact match, the caller would pass `ceil($min / 2)` as the parameter.

